Subject: [PATCH] webkit: trace auxiliary process launch and IPC connection open

The native PS5 title spawned its WebProcess and NetworkProcess but never
sent them a message (console run 22). Log, through the shell's logger when
it is linked (weak ps5_log_printf), when the launcher's completion runs on
the main run loop, when AuxiliaryProcessProxy::didFinishLaunching gets the
connection identifier and opens the connection, and when the PlayStation
SocketMonitor thread starts. PS5_HOMEBREW builds only; a no-op otherwise.

Also traced (console run 24: page updates never reached the screen):
DrawingAreaProxy Update messages, forced updates and incorporations without
setViewNeedsDisplay, update bitmaps that cannot be mapped, and failed
SharedMemory maps in the UI; the WebProcess side of Update and
PlayStationWebView::setViewNeedsDisplay are traced in patches 0013 and 0011
(the files they own).

Also traced (console run 25: the UI sent the page's WebProcess one message
and then nothing): the name of the first 40 messages sent and dispatched on
each connection, every waitForMessage, and sync replies that time out.

Also traced (console run 26: the page's WebProcess dispatched LoadRequest
but never CreateWebPage, which the UI had sent): every place
ConnectionUnix drops a message instead of sending or dispatching it (too
many attachments, an invalid descriptor attachment, no shared memory for an
out-of-line body, a missing or unmappable out-of-line body, a message that
cannot be decoded), and every out-of-line body sent or received.

Fixes for the native title (console run 27: "DROPS outgoing
WebProcess_CreateWebPage: no shared memory for its 7746-byte body (errno
1)"): SharedMemory::allocate sizes the object in whole 16 KiB pages and
falls back to an unlinked file in TMPDIR, logging each failed step; when no
shared memory can be had at all, a message up to 64 KiB is sent inline
instead of being dropped (receivers accept and buffer inline bodies that
large; the launcher's socket buffers are 256 KiB, patch 0005).

The out-of-line body is made with its own anonymous shm object whose only
descriptor goes into the message (console run 28: the title may not dup()
a descriptor, which SharedMemory::createHandle does).

Also traced (console run 29: "cookies are disabled" in the native title):
the NetworkProcess's cookie decisions (first party or page not allowed,
site not hosted, no storage session, the cookiesEnabled answer) and the
network session's kind and cookie database file.

SharedMemory::createHandle hands over the object's own descriptor when it
cannot be duplicated (native title), logging it.

Timing (console run 31: pages load very slowly in the native title): the
first 400 messages each way on a descriptor are logged with the
system-wide monotonic time at each hop (send, written by sendmsg,
received, dispatched), and every sendmsg that takes over 20 ms.

Routine traces (per message, per update, cookie decisions) are logged only
when the shell's ps5_trace_enabled() says so (PROSPEROWEB_TRACE=1): console
run 32 showed them stalling the children's run loops. Failures and one-time
events (process launch, connection open) are always logged (PS5_LOG).

Always on and cheap (console run 33, slow and partly rendered pages with
tracing off): every 5 s each process logs how many IPC messages it
dispatched and how long they waited after being received (median/p90 by
bucket, max), and the NetworkProcess how many resource loads started,
finished and failed, plus the first 20 failures.

Also: Connection::platformPrepareForOpen() opens the connection even when
the socket cannot be made non-blocking (logged). The PlayStation
SocketMonitor waits with select() before it reads, so a blocking socket
still works, while refusing to open left the child waiting forever (console
run 23, where fcntl on the socket was refused).
